diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/9115-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-add-IPv4-flowtable-offload.patch b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/9115-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-add-IPv4-flowtable-offload.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..201dd01
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/9115-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-add-IPv4-flowtable-offload.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,1816 @@
+From 15d46e4605ed0d7c7506d83b93db431629c3f669 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: OpenWrt-Xiaomi-RD16-port <rd16@localhost>
+Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:54:55 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: add IPv4 flowtable offload
+
+Offload IPv4 TCP/UDP flows from the netfilter flowtable to the PPE
+flow engine (TC_SETUP_FT). Each flow gets a flow table entry, a host
+entry for its source address and a nexthop that rewrites the MACs,
+the egress VLAN, and the NAT address and port. Packets that miss in
+the PPE, fragments and TCP control packets go to the CPU as before.
+
+Supported egress/ingress devices are the EDMA ports and DSA user
+ports of a switch using the yt921x-8021q tagger; the switch port is
+selected by the 802.1Q VID the tagger uses.
+
+Flow state and counters are in debugfs at ppe/flow.
+
+This is experimental and depends on QCOM_PPE_FLOW_OFFLOAD.
+---
